# ---- Secrets & env ---------------------------------------------------------
# Two complementary patterns: `.env*` covers `.env`, `.env.local`,
# `.env.production`, etc. (filename starts with .env). `*.env` covers
# `api.env`, `chatbot-py.env`, anything-named.env at any depth — the
# kind of stray file an editor or per-app loader sometimes drops next
# to the source. The negation `!*.env.example` keeps the canonical
# templates committed; the negation order matters (PASS, NEGATE, NEGATE).
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
# Per-developer launch configs (Claude Code, VS Code debug, etc.).
# A user-specific top-level `launch.json` MUST never reach the repo —
# it carries absolute paths, local API keys, and per-machine env
# overrides. The TRACKED `.claude/launch.json` is intentionally
# committed (shared team config, generic pnpm + vite invocation, no
# personal data).
/launch.json

# Per-developer docker-compose extensions go in
# docker-compose.local.yml (gitignored). The canonical
# docker-compose.override.yml IS committed (S1 reproducibility,
# ADR 0006) so a fresh clone yields a working stack out of the box.
docker-compose.local.yml
docker-compose.local.yaml

